    {
      "id": "g02",
      "title": {
        "t": "Wie viel kostet dieser Mantel?",
        "s": "this: dieser / diese / dieses"
      },
      "explain": "To point at something – *this* coat, *this* bag – use **dieser**. The ending matches the article: **der → dieser**, **die → diese**, **das → dieses**, plural **die → diese**.\nIn the accusative, masculine changes again, just like **den**: **Ich nehme diesen Mantel.**\nTo ask the price, say **Wie viel kostet …?** for one thing and **Wie viel kosten …?** for more than one: **Wie viel kosten diese Schuhe?**\nThe table shows: the word → *this* → *this* (accusative).",
      "table": [
        [
          "der Mantel",
          "dieser Mantel",
          "diesen Mantel"
        ],
        [
          "die Tasche",
          "diese Tasche",
          "diese Tasche"
        ],
        [
          "das Kleid",
          "dieses Kleid",
          "dieses Kleid"
        ],
        [
          "die Schuhe",
          "diese Schuhe",
          "diese Schuhe"
        ]
      ],
      "examples": [
